  "result": {
    "research": [
      {
        "topic": "sotn-decomp build environment and toolchain (reference workflow for a Brave Fencer Musashi PSX matching decomp)",
        "key_facts": [
          "Reference OS: Ubuntu 24.04 LTS (what sotn-decomp CI tests against; CI uses ubuntu-latest GitHub runners). On Windows, WSL2 is the documented path: PowerShell admin -> `dism.exe /online /enable-feature /featurename:VirtualMachinePlatform /all /norestart`, `Enable-WindowsOptionalFeature -Online -FeatureName \"Microsoft-Windows-Subsystem-Linux\" -NoRestart`, `wsl --install`, `wsl --set-default-version 2`, `wsl --install Ubuntu-24.04`. WSL1 fails with 'cannot execute binary file: Exec format error'.",
          "Setup sequence (from wiki Build page): `sudo apt-get update`; `sudo snap install --classic go`; `sudo apt-get install -y git`; `git clone https://github.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp.git`; `git submodule update --init --recursive`; `sudo apt-get install -y $(cat tools/requirements-debian.txt)`; `sudo apt-get install -y rustup && rustup default stable`; `make update-dependencies`; `rustup update`.",
          "tools/requirements-debian.txt (apt packages): bchunk, binutils-mipsel-linux-gnu, binutils-sh-elf, bsdmainutils, rustup, clang-format, coreutils, curl, gcc-mipsel-linux-gnu, git, libelf-dev, make, ninja-build, p7zip-full, python3-pip, python3-venv, unzip, wget, xfonts-utils. The cross toolchain is plain Debian/Ubuntu `binutils-mipsel-linux-gnu` + `gcc-mipsel-linux-gnu` (Arch users build AUR packages mipsel-linux-gnu-binutils / mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc with makepkg -si).",
          "Python deps go into a project-local venv (.venv, created by `make update-dependencies` via `python3 -m venv .venv` then `.venv/bin/pip3 install -r tools/requirements-python.txt`). Pinned versions in tools/requirements-python.txt: splat64==0.34.1, spimdisasm==1.35.0, rabbitizer==1.13.0, mapfile-parser==2.1.4, n64img==0.3.3, intervaltree==3.1.0, plus pre-commit, black, pycparser<3, watchdog, python-Levenshtein, cxxfilt, tabulate, requests, graphviz, crunch64, pygfxd, pillow, toml. splat is invoked as `.venv/bin/splat split <config yaml>`; per-overlay splat configs live in config/splat.us.<overlay>.yaml.",
          "Decomp tools are git submodules (.gitmodules): tools/asm-differ = https://github.com/simonlindholm/asm-differ.git; tools/m2c = https://github.com/matt-kempster/m2c.git; tools/maspsx = https://github.com/mkst/maspsx.git; tools/decomp-permuter = https://github.com/simonlindholm/decomp-permuter (pinned to commit b44b0622269fb4bff29e79fbbad26b9f47beda79); tools/mipsmatch = https://github.com/ttkb-oss/mipsmatch (Rust, cargo build --release); tools/mwccgap = https://github.com/mkst/mwccgap.git (PSP only); tools/saturn-splitter (Saturn only). m2ctx.py is curl-downloaded from https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ethteck/m2ctx/main/m2ctx.py.",
          "The 'gcc 2.6.3-psx' compiler is NOT apt gcc: it is a prebuilt Linux binary `bin/cc1-psx-26` downloaded by the Makefile from the GitHub release https://github.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/releases/download/cc1-psx-26/cc1-psx-26.tar.gz, verified against an in-repo bin/cc1-psx-26.tar.gz.sha256 via `sha256sum --check`. Per the release notes it is 'Build of GCC 2.6.3 with some minor patches to make it compatible with the PlayStation 1 hardware', compiled from https://github.com/decompals/old-gcc commit 370040a1b8510c752c8c91434309599c8857b97d. decompals/old-gcc is the canonical source for other vintage GCC versions if BFM used a different one (e.g. 2.7.2, 2.8.1).",
          "Exact PSX compile pipeline (from tools/builds/gen.py, which generates ninja rules): `mipsel-linux-gnu-cpp $cpp_flags -MMD -MF $out.d -lang-c -Iinclude -Iinclude/psxsdk -undef -Wall -fno-builtin <defines> $in | bin/cc1-psx-26 -G0 -w -funsigned-char -fpeephole -ffunction-cse -fpcc-struct-return -fcommon -fverbose-asm -msoft-float -g -quiet -mcpu=3000 -fgnu-linker -mgas -gcoff $cc_flags | python3 tools/maspsx/maspsx.py --expand-div --aspsx-version=$aspsx_ver | mipsel-linux-gnu-as -Iinclude -march=r3000 -mtune=r3000 -no-pad-sections -O1 -G0 -o $out`. So modern cpp preprocesses, vintage cc1 compiles to asm, maspsx massages the asm to emulate PsyQ's ASPSX assembler quirks, modern GNU as assembles. Defines include -Dmips -D__GNUC__=2 -D__OPTIMIZE__ -Dpsx -D_PSYQ -D_MIPSEL -D_LANGUAGE_C -DUSE_INCLUDE_ASM etc.",
          "Per-file compiler overrides: default CompilerParams are cc_opt=-O2, aspsx_ver=2.34. A `//!` comment in the first two lines of a .c file overrides them, e.g. `//! PSYQ=3.3 O=1` (PSYQ=3.3 -> maspsx --aspsx-version=2.21, PSYQ=3.5 -> 2.34; O=N -> -ON). Linking: `mipsel-linux-gnu-ld -nostdlib --no-check-sections -Map $map_out -T <linker script from splat> -o $out`, then `mipsel-linux-gnu-objcopy -O binary` to produce the raw PSX exe/overlay binaries.",
          "Makefile flow (orchestration recently moved into a Go tool; `./sotn.sh` is just `go run ./tools/sotn-assets \"$@\"`): 1) `make extract_disk` — sotn-disk (Go) extracts files from disks/sotn.us.cue into disks/us/; 2) `make extract -j` — runs `./sotn.sh extract-assets config/assets.us.yaml` + splat to produce asm/us/, assets/, linker scripts; 3) `make build -j` — `./sotn.sh build us`, which generates ninja build graph and compiles into build/us/, then automatically runs the checksum check (skippable with SKIP_CHECK=1); 4) `make check` / `./sotn.sh check us` — SHA1 verification; 5) `make expected` — after a green build, copies build/us -> expected/build/us as the asm-differ baseline; 6) `make clean` needed whenever config/ changes; 7) `make disk` rebuilds a runnable CUE/BIN. VERSION env selects target (default us): `VERSION=us make ...`.",
          "Checksum ('OK') verification mechanics (tools/sotn-assets/check.go): config/check.us.sha contains lines of `<sha1hex>  build/us/<FILE>` (e.g. `54828d4e44ea9575f2a0917ff63def42a304abff  build/us/main.exe`, plus DRA.BIN, RIC.BIN, every stage overlay and F_* file). The Go check command SHA1-hashes each built artifact and compares case-insensitively; any mismatch fails the build with 'checksum check failed'. This is the matching-decomp ground truth. Separately, `make expected` maintains the expected/build/<version> tree that asm-differ's diff.py uses as the comparison baseline (-o flag family).",
          "Per-function workflow (wiki Decompilation page) — recommended aliases: `alias sotn=\"make clean && make -j extract && make -j build && make expected\"`; `alias dec=\".venv/bin/python3 ./tools/decompile.py\"` (wraps m2ctx + m2c to produce a first-pass C translation and can upload to decomp.me); `alias differ=\".venv/bin/python3 ./tools/asm-differ/diff.py -mow3 --overlay\"`. Flow: find `INCLUDE_ASM(\"st/wrp/nonmatchings/6FD0\", func_801873A0);` in source -> `dec func_801873A0` -> `differ st/wrp func_801873A0` -> iterate C until asm matches -> rebuild, check stays green. decomp.me preset: compiler 'gcc 2.6.3-psx + maspsx', context generated by `SOURCE=src/dra/42398.c make context` (runs m2ctx, writes ctx.c). decomp-permuter used for stubborn mismatches.",
          "Language/runtime versions: Python >= 3.12.x required (wiki troubleshooting: f-string SyntaxError on older versions; Ubuntu 24.04 ships 3.12). Go >= 1.24.0 (tools/sotn-assets/go.mod 'go 1.24.0'; CI uses go-version-file: go.work). Rust: rustup stable channel (used for mipsmatch, tools/dups, tools/sotn_str — auxiliary tooling, not the core compile pipeline). ninja-build required (build graph is ninja, generated by tools/builds/gen.py).",
          "Disc image requirements: unmodified retail dump as BIN/CUE placed in disks/, cue named sotn.<version>.cue (sotn.us.cue for default). For BFM the analog would be a SLUS-00726 BIN/CUE. Dumping recipe: `sudo apt install -y cdrdao toc2cue; cdrdao read-cd --read-raw --datafile sotn.us.bin --device /dev/sr0 --driver generic-mmc-raw sotn.us.toc; toc2cue sotn.us.toc sotn.us.cue`.",
          "Non-matching escape hatch: code wrapped in `#ifndef NON_MATCHING` can be built with `CPP_FLAGS=-DNON_MATCHING make`; cpp defs also include -DUSE_INCLUDE_ASM and gen.py supports a SKIP_ASM=1 define mode. `make force_symbols` regenerates the full symbol list from a successful build; `make force_extract` re-extracts all asm regardless of decomp status.",
          "The cc1-psx-26 GitHub release also hosts the other-platform compilers (mwccpsp_219 / mwccpsp_3.0.1_147 for PSP via wibo, cygnus-2.7-96Q3 GCCSH for Saturn, binutils-allegrex) — irrelevant to a PSX-only BFM project; the PSX-only subset is: mipsel-linux-gnu binutils+cpp, cc1-psx-26 (or other old-gcc build), maspsx, splat, ninja, python venv.",
          "Tool roles as documented in README: splat disassembles/splits the binary using symbol configs; m2c (mips2c) converts MIPS asm to C; asm-differ compares current build vs expected baseline; decomp-permuter auto-permutes C to find matches; maspsx replicates PSX SDK (ASPSX) assembler behavior on top of GNU as; decomp.me for collaborative scratches; frogress (decomp.dev) stores progress data (progress.py uploads with FROGRESS_API_BASE_URL/FROGRESS_API_SECRET env vars in CI)."
        ],
        "workflow_steps": [
          "Install WSL2 Ubuntu 24.04 on the Windows 11 host (wsl --set-default-version 2; wsl --install Ubuntu-24.04).",
          "Inside WSL: sudo apt-get update; sudo snap install --classic go; sudo apt-get install -y git; clone repo; git submodule update --init --recursive.",
          "sudo apt-get install -y $(cat tools/requirements-debian.txt); sudo apt-get install -y rustup; rustup default stable.",
          "make update-dependencies (creates .venv, pip-installs pinned splat64/spimdisasm/etc., inits asm-differ/m2c/maspsx/mipsmatch submodules, downloads m2ctx.py, downloads+sha256-verifies bin/cc1-psx-26 tarball from the cc1-psx-26 GitHub release, go-builds bin/sotn-disk, cargo-builds Rust helpers); rustup update.",
          "Place retail BIN/CUE dump in disks/ named sotn.us.cue (BFM equivalent: the SLUS-00726 dump).",
          "make extract_disk  (sotn-disk extracts ISO contents to disks/us/).",
          "make extract -j  (splat splits exe+overlays per config/splat.us.*.yaml into asm/, generates linker scripts; assets extracted per config/assets.us.yaml).",
          "make build -j  (ninja graph from tools/builds/gen.py compiles: mipsel-linux-gnu-cpp | bin/cc1-psx-26 | maspsx.py --expand-div --aspsx-version=2.34 | mipsel-linux-gnu-as; links with mipsel-linux-gnu-ld -T <splat .ld>; objcopy -O binary).",
          "make check  (Go tool SHA1-compares every build/us artifact against config/check.us.sha; any mismatch = failure).",
          "make expected  (snapshot build/us into expected/build/us as the asm-differ baseline).",
          "Per function: locate INCLUDE_ASM stub -> .venv/bin/python3 tools/decompile.py <func> (m2ctx+m2c first pass) -> .venv/bin/python3 tools/asm-differ/diff.py -mow3 --overlay <ovl> <func> -> iterate C until match -> rebuild, confirm check still green; use decomp-permuter or decomp.me (preset 'gcc 2.6.3-psx + maspsx', context via SOURCE=<file> make context) for hard mismatches.",
          "make clean whenever config/ yaml or symbol files change, then re-extract/rebuild."
        ],
        "tools_required": [
          "WSL2 + Ubuntu 24.04 LTS (mandatory on Windows; install via wsl --install Ubuntu-24.04)",
          "GNU Make + ninja-build (apt) — Make is the entry point, ninja executes the build graph generated by tools/builds/gen.py",
          "binutils-mipsel-linux-gnu + gcc-mipsel-linux-gnu (apt) — provides mipsel-linux-gnu-cpp/as/ld/objcopy (modern cross binutils; the vintage compiler is separate)",
          "cc1-psx-26 — patched GCC 2.6.3 cc1 for PS1, prebuilt Linux binary auto-downloaded by make update-dependencies from https://github.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/releases/tag/cc1-psx-26 (source: https://github.com/decompals/old-gcc @ 370040a1); other GCC versions for BFM available from decompals/old-gcc",
          "Python >= 3.12 + python3-venv/python3-pip (apt); project venv at .venv with pinned pip packages: splat64==0.34.1, spimdisasm==1.35.0, rabbitizer==1.13.0, mapfile-parser==2.1.4, pycparser<3, intervaltree==3.1.0, n64img==0.3.3, etc.",
          "splat (pip splat64) — binary splitting/disassembly driven by config/splat.<ver>.<overlay>.yaml",
          "maspsx (git submodule, https://github.com/mkst/maspsx) — Python filter emulating PsyQ ASPSX; invoked as maspsx.py --expand-div --aspsx-version={2.21|2.34}",
          "m2c (git submodule, https://github.com/matt-kempster/m2c) + m2ctx.py (from ethteck/m2ctx) + tools/decompile.py wrapper — asm-to-C first pass",
          "asm-differ (git submodule, https://github.com/simonlindholm/asm-differ) — diff.py -mow3 --overlay, compares against expected/build/<ver> baseline",
          "decomp-permuter (git submodule pinned to commit b44b0622269fb4bff29e79fbbad26b9f47beda79, https://github.com/simonlindholm/decomp-permuter)",
          "Go >= 1.24.0 (snap install --classic go) — builds/runs tools/sotn-assets orchestrator (build/check/clean/extract-assets/disk/objdiff subcommands) and bin/sotn-disk",
          "Rust stable via rustup (apt rustup; rustup default stable) — auxiliary tools: mipsmatch (function fingerprint matching), dups (duplicate-function report), sotn_str",
          "cdrdao + toc2cue (apt, optional) — disc dumping to BIN/CUE",
          "objdiff (optional, via ./sotn.sh objdiff / objdiff-gui) and gobindiff (./sotn.sh bindiff) — alternative diff frontends"
        ],
        "windows_vs_linux": "Native Windows is NOT supported; the project documents only Ubuntu 24.04 (CI: ubuntu-latest) and tells Windows users to use WSL2 explicitly. Hard Linux dependencies: bin/cc1-psx-26 is a prebuilt Linux ELF executable; the cross toolchain comes from apt (binutils-mipsel-linux-gnu, gcc-mipsel-linux-gnu); the Makefile requires bash (-e -o pipefail) and the whole pipe-based compile rule assumes POSIX; wibo (Windows-PE-on-Linux loader, used only for PSP's mwccpsp) further assumes Linux. Pieces that are theoretically portable (pure Python: splat, maspsx, m2c, asm-differ, decomp-permuter; Go tools) do not make the build runnable natively because of cc1-psx-26 and the apt cross-binutils. Practical setup for the BFM project: keep Ghidra + the MCP server + Claude Code on native Windows 11, and run the decomp repo (extract/build/check) inside WSL2 Ubuntu 24.04, sharing the working tree via the WSL filesystem (note: keep the repo inside the WSL ext4 filesystem, not /mnt/c, for tolerable build performance). The wiki troubleshooting confirms WSL1 specifically breaks on cc1-psx-26 (Exec format error).",
        "risks_gotchas": [
          "The wiki's `make check` is stale terminology: in the current repo there is no standalone Makefile check target — `./sotn.sh build` runs the SHA1 check automatically at the end (set SKIP_CHECK=1 to bypass), and `./sotn.sh check [version|all]` runs it standalone. The Makefile's only sha-related rule is the sha256 verification of downloaded toolchain tarballs.",
          "sotn-decomp's build orchestration was recently rewritten in Go (tools/sotn-assets via sotn.sh) + ninja; older blog posts/wiki snapshots (including mathisto.github.io mirror) describe a pure-Make flow. When copying patterns for BFM, copy from the current master, and expect docs to lag the code.",
          "GCC 2.6.3 is SOTN-specific (1997 title). Brave Fencer Musashi (mid-1998, Square) very likely used a different PsyQ/GCC version (commonly 2.7.2 or 2.8.1-era ccpsx) — the exact compiler+ASPSX version must be determined empirically (compiler fingerprinting, decomp.me preset experiments) before any of the cc1 flags can be trusted. maspsx --aspsx-version must match the game's PsyQ release (SOTN uses 2.21 for PSYQ 3.3 files, 2.34 for 3.5).",
          "splat must run from the venv; a common failure is `splat: command not found` because .venv/bin (or ~/.local/bin) is not on PATH — the Makefile handles this by invoking .venv/bin/splat directly.",
          "Python older than 3.12 fails mid-build with f-string SyntaxError; Ubuntu 22.04 default python3 (3.10) is insufficient — use Ubuntu 24.04.",
          "expected/ baseline and check shas are two different verification layers: asm-differ silently diffs against a stale expected/build if you forget to re-run `make expected` after pulling/building; the SHA1 check only validates final binaries, not individual objects.",
          "Any change to config/ (splat yamls, symbol files) requires `make clean` before re-extracting, or stale asm/linker scripts cause confusing mismatches.",
          "decomp-permuter submodule is pinned to a specific commit (b44b0622...) — blindly updating submodules can break tooling.",
          "The 7900-line check.us.sha-style ground truth assumes a specific known-good dump; a BFM project must first generate its own per-file SHA1 manifest from a verified SLUS-00726 dump (cross-check against redump.org hashes).",
          "GitHub release binaries (cc1-psx-26.tar.gz) are x86-64 Linux; on ARM hosts or macOS they will not run — sotn-decomp CI and docs assume x86-64 Ubuntu."
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "Which exact compiler (GCC version / PsyQ SDK release / ASPSX version) was used to build Brave Fencer Musashi SLUS-00726 — needs fingerprinting (e.g. compiling known SDK functions at -O2 with candidate old-gcc builds, or checking decomp.me presets for other 1998 Square PSX titles).",
          "Whether maspsx fully covers the ASPSX version BFM's PsyQ release used, or whether different maspsx flags (--expand-div etc.) are needed.",
          "Whether macOS is even partially supported (Makefile detects Darwin but the wiki documents only Ubuntu; cc1-psx-26 release ships Linux binaries only) — irrelevant if we commit to WSL2.",
          "How well splat handles BFM's overlay scheme (SOTN drives one splat yaml per overlay; BFM's overlay/file layout on disc is different and must be mapped first).",
          "Performance/ergonomics of bridging native-Windows Ghidra MCP with a WSL2-resident build tree (file sharing, path translation, watch tooling)."
        ],
