      {
        "topic": "sotn-decomp per-function matching decompilation workflow and SOTN PS1 internals (as architectural template for a Brave Fencer Musashi SLUS-00726 decomp)",
        "key_facts": [
          "PER-FUNCTION LOOP (sotn-decomp): (1) pick function from auto-generated difficulty list, (2) find its INCLUDE_ASM line in src, (3) run tools/decompile.py (m2c wrapper) which REPLACES the INCLUDE_ASM line in the .c file with m2c output, (4) run asm-differ in watch mode and iterate the C until asm matches, (5) optionally use decomp.me and decomp-permuter for stubborn mismatches, (6) clean up/rename, run full build check, PR.",
          "Convenience aliases used by the project (from wiki/Decompilation): alias sotn=\"make clean && make -j extract && make -j build && make expected\" ; alias dec=\".venv/bin/python3 ./tools/decompile.py\" ; alias differ=\".venv/bin/python3 ./tools/asm-differ/diff.py -mow3 --overlay\". Usage: `dec func_801873A0` then `differ st/wrp func_801873A0` (left pane = target asm, right = current build; -m rebuild, -o diff vs object, -w watch, -3 three-way).",
          "tools/decompile.py specifics: args = function name, --version/-v (default $VERSION or 'us'), --overlay/-o (disambiguate when same func name exists in several overlays), --upload/-u (push scratch to decomp.me). It rglob-searches asm/<version>/**/nonmatchings/**/<func>.s, builds a context via m2ctx.import_c_file(), and invokes m2c with flags: -P 4 --pointer-style left --knr --indent-switch-contents --comment-style oneline --target mipsel-gcc-c --context <tmp_ctx>. Output is written in-place into the C file via safe temp-file + os.replace().",
          "Function difficulty list: CI generates functions.md on the 'gh-duplicates' branch (https://github.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/blob/gh-duplicates/functions.md). Columns: Ovl | Function | Length | Branches | Jtbl | Duplicate(Full/Part link to duplicates.txt) | WIP | %. Pick short functions with few branches; check Jtbl column (jump tables need extra steps) and Duplicate column (don't re-match duplicates). duplicates.txt lives at https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/gh-duplicates/duplicates.txt; `make duplicates-report`/`make duplicates` run a cargo (Rust) similarity tool with default threshold 0.90.",
          "decomp.me loop: generate context with `SOURCE=path/to/my/function.c make context` (Makefile recipe: VERSION=$(VERSION) $(M2CTX) $(SOURCE), producing ctx.c). On decomp.me: Platform=PlayStation, Compiler=`gcc 2.6.3-psx + maspsx`, Preset='Castlevania: Symphony of the Night'; paste ctx.c into Context pane and the function's .s into Target assembly, Create scratch. decompile.py -u automates scratch upload.",
          "INCLUDE_ASM mechanics (include/include_asm.h): #define INCLUDE_ASM(FOLDER, NAME) __asm__(\".pushsection .text\" ... \".globl \" #NAME \".NON_MATCHING\" ... \".include \\\"asm/\" VERSION \"/\" FOLDER \"/\" #NAME \".s\\\"\" ...) — i.e. the raw splat-extracted .s is assembled into the C TU. INCLUDE_RODATA does the same into .rodata. NON_MATCHING ifdef convention: wrap logically-correct-but-unmatched C in the NON_MATCHING preprocessor guard so default (matching) builds use INCLUDE_ASM and `CPP_FLAGS=-DNON_MATCHING make` compiles the C instead (same-author convention, croc README confirms the -DNON_MATCHING build switch).",
          "SPLAT CONFIG, main exe (config/splat.us.main.yaml) options block verbatim: platform: psx; basename: main; base_path: ..; build_path: build/us; target_path: disks/us/SLUS_000.67; asm_path: asm/us/main; asset_path: assets/main; src_path: src/main; ld_script_path: build/us/main.ld; compiler: GCC; symbol_addrs_path: [config/symbols.us.txt, config/symbols.us.main.txt]; create_undefined_funcs_auto: no; undefined_funcs_auto_path: build/us/config/undefined_funcs_auto.us.main.txt; create_undefined_syms_auto: yes; undefined_syms_auto_path: ...; find_file_boundaries: yes; use_legacy_include_asm: no; asm_jtbl_label_macro: jlabel; disassemble_all: true; global_vram_start: 0x80010000; section_order: ['.rodata','.text','.data','.bss']; ld_generate_symbol_per_data_segment: true. Segments: PSX exe header at 0x0, then one 'code'-type segment start: 0x800, vram: 0x80010000 with subsegments like [0x800, .rodata, main], [0x15F4, asm, psxsdk/2mbyte], [0x16B8, c, main], [0x1BCE0, data], [0x241E8, .bss, main].",
          "SPLAT CONFIG, overlays: one yaml PER overlay per version (config/splat.us.dra.yaml, splat.us.stwrp.yaml, splat.us.ric.yaml, splat.us.weapon.yaml, splat.us.tt_000.yaml...). DRA: basename dra; target_path disks/us/DRA.BIN; asm_path asm/us/dra; src_path src/dra; extensions_path tools/splat_ext; one 'code' segment start 0x0, vram 0x800A0000 (90+ subsegments of .data/.rodata/c/.bss) plus a 'data'-type segment at start 0x9B6A0 vram 0x8013B6A0. Stage overlay stwrp: vram 0x80180000, single code segment ordered .data -> .rodata -> .text(c files) -> .bss, subalign 4. Each yaml stacks two symbol files: shared config/symbols.us.txt + per-overlay config/symbols.us.<ovl>.txt.",
          "SYMBOL MANAGEMENT: symbol_addrs files use splat format `name = 0xADDRESS;` with optional trailing annotations like `// size:0x300` (example verbatim: g_CastleFlags = 0x8003BDEC; // size:0x300). Prefixes: func_<vram> (undecompiled), g_ globals, s_ statics, jpt_ jump tables, a... auto-named string/array data, D_<vram> raw data. Renaming = edit the symbols .txt then re-run extract; never hand-edit generated asm. `make force_symbols` regenerates a full symbol list from a successful build. Style (docs/STYLE.md): functions PascalCase (UpdateAccel), globals g_PascalCase, statics s_PascalCase, struct members camelCase, enums SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE, 4-space indent, 80 cols, `s32* var` pointer style, clang-format enforced via `make format`.",
          "DUPLICATE FUNCTIONS across overlays (wiki/Deduplication): functions WITHOUT data — add the named symbol (e.g. CheckColliderOffsets) to each stage's symbols.us.<ovl>.txt at that overlay's own address, factor the C body into a shared header, and `#include` that header from each overlay's C file (see PR #1200). Functions WITH data — additionally name every referenced datum in each overlay's symbols file (some stages required renaming PfnEntityUpdates) (see PR #459). The Duplicate column in functions.md flags Full/Part duplicates so effort is spent once.",
          "SOTN OVERLAY ARCHITECTURE (template): SLUS_000.67 (main.exe) loaded by BIOS at 0x80010000 (0x80010000-0x8009FFFF) contains ONLY Psy-Q hardware API (pad, CD, memcard, GPU) + bootstrap; it loads DRA.BIN + F_MAP.BIN and jumps to the engine. Memory map: DRA.BIN game engine 0x800A0000-0x8013BFFF; ARC_F.BIN (player sprites) 0x8013C000-0x8016FFFF (RIC.BIN alternate-character overlay occupies 0x8013C000-0x8017FFFF); WEAPON0/1.BIN 0x8017A000-0x8017FFFF; stage overlays ST/*/*.BIN 0x80180000-0x801DFFFF (80+ stage IDs 0x00-0x4F); F_MAP.BIN 0x801E0000-0x801E8000; heap/stack 0x801F0000-0x801F7800. Inter-overlay calls go through a shared `GameApi` function-pointer struct statically allocated by main.exe — overlays never call each other directly. File loading uses hard-coded LBA lookup tables (stage offsets/sizes at 0x800A3C40, general files at 0x800ACC74); the sotn-disk tool patches LBA tables post-build; a dev-only 'sim:' driver loads overlays from HDD.",
          "JUMP TABLES: splat option asm_jtbl_label_macro: jlabel. On decomp.me, append the jtbl after the function asm under `.section .rodata` with `.set noat` / `.set noreorder` at top. In-repo: run `python3 tools/split_jpt_yaml/split_jpt_yaml.py config/splat.us.dra.yaml asm/us/dra/data/ jpt_` and paste its 'Cut below this line:' output into the yaml subsegments; then change `[0x4208C, rodata] # jpt_80133C10` to `[0x4208C, .rodata, 93BDC]` (leading dot = linker uses the compiler-generated table instead of extracted asm).",
          "REGISTER-MISMATCH TRICKS (wiki): prefer `foo > 0x28` over `foo >= 0x29` (compiler emits slti with +1); a dangling `li v0,0x80` before loads signals `index = foo % 0x80;`; redundant MOVE rX,rX can be forced with arithmetic that cancels (`(Random() & 3) + 1 - 1`); declaring a callee `static` in the same TU changes register allocation before calls; mark unavoidable hacks with `// !FAKE:` and bugs with `//! @bug`.",
          "BUILD SYSTEM: `make extract_disk` (dump files from .cue/.bin placed at disks/sotn.us.cue — exact name required), `make extract` (splat disassembly per yaml), `make build`, `make check` (sha/objdiff vs original), `make expected` (snapshot build to expected/build/$VERSION for asm-differ baselines), `make context`, `make force_symbols`, `make format`. Multi-version via `export VERSION=us|hd|pspeu|saturn` (default us). Toolchain: GNU make + mipsel-linux-gnu binutils + gcc 2.6.3-psx (via maspsx wrapper) + splat + python venv (.venv) + go (sotn-assets asset pipeline, sotn.sh is just `go run ./tools/sotn-assets \"$@\"`) + rust/cargo (duplicates tool) + dosemu debs (DOS-era tooling). Setup: `sudo apt-get install -y $(cat tools/requirements-debian.txt)`; rustup; `sudo dpkg -i tools/dosemu-deb/*.deb`; `git submodule update --init --recursive`. Python 3.12+ required.",
          "Progress dashboards: https://sotn.xee.dev/ renders per-overlay matched-percentage; functions.md WIP/% columns track per-function state. The mathisto.github.io/sotn-wiki pages are an unofficial mirror of the canonical GitHub wiki (24 pages; key ones: Decompilation, Internals, Build, Deduplication, Decompiling-functions-with-jump-tables, Register-Mismatch-Decompilation-Tricks, Pull-Request-Guidelines, Importing-Data)."
        ],
        "workflow_steps": [
          "One-time: build clean baseline — `make clean && make -j extract && make -j build && make expected` (the 'sotn' alias) and confirm `make check` passes OK for every binary.",
          "Pick a target function from the difficulty-sorted functions.md (gh-duplicates branch): prefer short Length / few Branches, no Jtbl flag; skip or dedupe anything marked Duplicate; check last column for an existing decomp.me scratch to resume.",
          "Locate the function: global-search the name to find its `INCLUDE_ASM(\"st/wrp/nonmatchings/6FD0\", func_801873A0);` line in src/.",
          "Scaffold C with m2c: `dec func_801873A0` (tools/decompile.py) — auto-builds context, runs m2c (-P 4 --knr --pointer-style left --target mipsel-gcc-c), and replaces the INCLUDE_ASM line in the .c file with the draft.",
          "Start the diff loop: `differ st/wrp func_801873A0` (asm-differ diff.py -mow3 --overlay) — watch mode rebuilds on save and shows target asm (left) vs current build (right).",
          "Iterate the C (types, control flow shape, register-mismatch tricks like >0x28 vs >=0x29, static callees, temp variables) until the diff is instruction- and regalloc-identical.",
          "If stuck: `SOURCE=src/st/wrp/6FD0.c make context` to produce ctx.c, create a decomp.me scratch (PlayStation / gcc 2.6.3-psx + maspsx / SOTN preset) for collaborative iteration; and/or run decomp-permuter: `./import.py path/to/file.c path/to/func.s` then `./permuter.py -j<N> nonmatching/<dir>/` hunting for score 0.",
          "If truly unmatchable now: keep the C under the NON_MATCHING guard (default build keeps INCLUDE_ASM; `CPP_FLAGS=-DNON_MATCHING make` compiles the C) rather than blocking.",
          "On match: rename func_/D_ symbols meaningfully in config/symbols.us.<ovl>.txt (PascalCase functions, g_ globals), re-extract, `make format`, full `sotn` rebuild + `make check`, commit, PR.",
          "If the function is duplicated across overlays: match it once, move the body to a shared header, add the per-overlay addresses to each symbols.us.<ovl>.txt, and #include the header from every overlay that contains it."
        ],
        "tools_required": [
          "splat (pip, in .venv) — disassembly/splitting driven by one yaml per binary/overlay; needs platform: psx, asm_jtbl_label_macro: jlabel, extensions_path for custom segment types",
          "m2c (matching-decomp decompiler, python; sotn pins it as a submodule/tool under tools/) — invoked via tools/decompile.py wrapper with --target mipsel-gcc-c",
          "asm-differ (simonlindholm; sotn vendors a fork at tools/asm-differ with an --overlay option) — run as .venv/bin/python3 tools/asm-differ/diff.py -mow3 --overlay <ovl> <func>",
          "decomp-permuter (https://github.com/simonlindholm/decomp-permuter) — ./import.py file.c file.s; ./permuter.py -j dir/; pip deps pycparser, toml, optional pynacl (permuter@home -J), Levenshtein; score 0 = match",
          "decomp.me (web) — PlayStation platform, compiler 'gcc 2.6.3-psx + maspsx' for SOTN; context generated by `SOURCE=... make context` (tools/m2ctx.py)",
          "gcc 2.6.3-psx cross compiler + maspsx assembler shim + mipsel-linux-gnu binutils (GNU as/ld) — the matching toolchain",
          "GNU make + ninja (linker-script regen in force_symbols) + python 3.12+ venv + go (asset pipeline) + rust/cargo (duplicates detector) + clang-format + dosemu (tools/dosemu-deb/*.deb)",
          "sotn-disk (project tool) — rebuilds/patches the disc image LBA tables post-build; equivalent needed for BFM disc rebuild",
          "For the BFM project itself: Ghidra + Ghidra MCP server (runs natively on Windows) alongside the WSL2 build/match loop"
        ],
        "windows_vs_linux": "The sotn-decomp build/match loop is Linux-only in practice: documented platform is Ubuntu 24.04 LTS (WSL2 explicitly fine), installed via `sudo apt-get install -y $(cat tools/requirements-debian.txt)` plus rustup and `sudo dpkg -i tools/dosemu-deb/*.deb`; it depends on mipsel-linux-gnu binutils, dosemu, make, and shell scripts. So for BFM: run splat, the gcc/psyq cross compiler, maspsx, asm-differ, m2c, and decomp-permuter inside WSL2 with the repo on the Linux filesystem (not /mnt/z) for performance. Natively on Windows: Ghidra + the Ghidra MCP server, the browser for decomp.me (compilation is server-side, OS-independent), and Claude Code itself; m2c and splat are pure Python and can run on Windows in a pinch, but the make-driven extract/build/check/expected loop and asm-differ watch mode should live in WSL2. Note the host repo is on Z:\\ — a WSL2 clone under ~/ is strongly advised.",
        "risks_gotchas": [
          "WebFetch returns model-summarized page content; most commands above were cross-checked across the mirror, the canonical GitHub wiki, and raw repo files, but treat long verbatim yaml/macro quotes as 'verify in repo' (clone and grep before hard-coding into the project doc).",
          "NON_MATCHING polarity is easy to get backwards: the guard keeps unmatched C OUT of the default (matching) build; `CPP_FLAGS=-DNON_MATCHING make` compiles it in. The exact #ifdef/#else/INCLUDE_ASM arrangement was confirmed conceptually (wiki + croc README by the same author) but I did not capture a verbatim in-repo example.",
          "asm-differ's `--overlay` flag is sotn-fork-specific (not in upstream simonlindholm/asm-differ); for BFM you will need either their fork or `-o` object-diff mode, because overlay code is not at its load address inside the file on disc.",
          "SOTN matches with gcc 2.6.3-psx + maspsx, but Brave Fencer Musashi (1998, Square) almost certainly uses a different PSY-Q toolchain (likely SN-gcc 2.7.x / psyq 4.x with ASPSX) — the SOTN decomp.me preset and compiler flags will NOT transfer; compiler identification for SLUS-00726 is a prerequisite step (try candidate compilers on a few functions via decomp.me).",
          "Jump-table functions break the naive loop: splat must have asm_jtbl_label_macro set and the jtbl rodata must be re-homed to the C file's .rodata subsegment (leading-dot `[offset, .rodata, file]` syntax) or the build links duplicate tables.",
          "find_file_boundaries: yes makes splat guess file splits; expect to manually adjust subsegment offsets as functions get matched (wrong splits cause rodata/text misattribution and link failures).",
          "Duplicate functions across overlays are a major efficiency trap for an overlay-heavy game: without a duplicates detector (sotn uses a cargo tool, threshold 0.90, output on gh-duplicates branch) you will re-match the same code dozens of times; SOTN's fix is shared headers + per-overlay symbol addresses, which also means one symbol name maps to MANY addresses — keep per-overlay symbols files separate from day one.",
          "decompile.py edits source files in place (replaces the INCLUDE_ASM line); under an MCP/Claude-driven loop, commit before running it so a bad m2c scaffold is trivially revertable.",
          "Overlapping overlay VRAM ranges (e.g. RIC.BIN vs ARC_F+WEAPON at 0x8013C000) mean Ghidra needs either per-overlay programs or overlay memory blocks; a single flat address space will mis-attribute symbols — same issue will arise in BFM if it swaps overlays at a shared address.",
          "SOTN's MAD.BIN debug overlay was compiled against an older DRA.BIN, so its pointers are stale — when sampling overlays in a new game, don't assume every overlay on disc matches the shipped engine's symbol addresses."
        ],
        "open_questions": [
          "Which compiler/assembler shipped Brave Fencer Musashi SLUS-00726 (psyq 4.0/4.1 gcc 2.7.2? aspsx version?) — must be identified empirically before any matching is possible; does decomp.me already have a BFM or Square-1998 preset?",
          "Does BFM use a SOTN-style overlay system (separate .BIN overlays loaded at fixed VRAM) or a monolithic exe + data archives? Determines whether the multi-yaml splat layout is needed at all.",
          "Exact in-repo NON_MATCHING usage example and whether sotn-decomp's CI builds both matching and -DNON_MATCHING variants.",
          "Details of sotn's asm-differ fork --overlay implementation (worth porting for BFM overlay diffing).",
          "How `make extract` orchestrates splat across all the per-overlay yamls (the Makefile excerpt showed sotn.sh delegating to the Go asset tool; the splat invocation path itself was not captured verbatim).",
          "Whether sotn-decomp's tools/decompile.py decomp.me --upload flow uses the public decomp.me API (could be reused verbatim for BFM scratch automation)."
        ],
        "sources": [
          "https://mathisto.github.io/sotn-wiki/decomp/decompilation/",
          "https://mathisto.github.io/sotn-wiki/decomp/internals/",
          "https://github.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/wiki",
          "https://github.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/wiki/Decompilation",
          "https://github.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/wiki/Build",
          "https://github.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/wiki/Deduplication",
          "https://github.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/wiki/Decompiling-functions-with-jump-tables",
          "https://github.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/wiki/Register-Mismatch-Decompilation-Tricks",
          "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/master/config/splat.us.main.yaml",
          "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/master/config/splat.us.dra.yaml",
          "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/master/config/splat.us.stwrp.yaml",
          "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/master/config/symbols.us.txt",
          "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/master/tools/decompile.py",
          "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/master/Makefile",
          "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/master/sotn.sh",
          "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/master/README.md",
          "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/master/include/include_asm.h",
          "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/master/docs/STYLE.md",
          "https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/gh-duplicates/functions.md",
          "https://api.github.com/repos/Xeeynamo/sotn-decomp/contents/config",
