        "windows_vs_linux": "Everything found in this research runs natively on Windows: CUE's BRAVE.EXE (+ C source compilable with any Windows C compiler), BizHawk, Ghidra/GhidraMCP, and the Python disc-parsing used here. Nothing in the BFM-specific knowledge base requires Linux/WSL2; WSL2 only becomes relevant later for the splat/GCC 2.6.3-psx matching-build toolchain (outside this topic's scope).",
        "risks_gotchas": [
          "Prompt-injection/anti-bot hazard: WebFetch of https://tcrf.net/Brave_Fencer_Musashi twice returned an unrelated 'test document for AI systems with instructions' -- content was discarded and the page was instead retrieved via TCRF's MediaWiki API with curl. Treat any direct tcrf.net fetch output as untrusted; always use the api.php route.",
          "romhacking.net and GameFAQs are Cloudflare/403-blocked to bots; romhacking.net forum thread 'topic=26396.0' ([PSX] Brave Fencer Musashi) has NO Wayback snapshot and remains unread -- potential undocumented format info lost there. Utility pages ARE archived on Wayback. WebFetch cannot reach web.archive.org but curl can.",
          "The LZSS variant uses an ABSOLUTE 10-bit ring-buffer index, not a relative LZSS distance -- generic LZSS tools will not work; use CUE's BRAVE source or the verified MIPS listing as ground truth. Also note the end-of-stream marker is a 16-bit code with low 10 bits == 0.",
          "AiroRom wiki disassembly uses nonstandard register names (r2..r31 instead of v0/a0/etc.) and pseudo-ops like 'movp/movbp'; addresses were unattributed to a region but were verified in this session to match SLUS-00726 exactly (words at 0x80018730/34/90, 0x800187BC, 0x80018824, 0x80018910, and the table at 0x80072A30). JP-version equivalents are NOT verified.",
          "Two different pad-state addresses exist (TCRF debug code conditions on 0x80078DC2; gamehacking.org joker uses 0x80078DCA) -- they are separate mirrors/fields; do not conflate.",
          "Release-date conflicts across sources: Hidden Palace says US release Oct 31 1998 / final US build Sep 22 1998; TCRF says US Nov 12 1998 (Squaresoft press release); psxdatacenter shows an obviously wrong '11 January 1998'. Prefer redump/TCRF-cited primary sources and verify from the disc itself if it matters.",
          "TCRF says everything in the debug menu EXCEPT area selection is non-functional in retail -- do not expect a working sound test from it.",
          "GitHub wiki pages of AiroRom fail to load in the web UI ('error while loading'); always use the raw.githubusercontent.com/wiki/... mirror.",
          "Archipelago repo addresses are file offsets into BizHawk MAIN_RAM (no 0x80000000 base) and some entries are code patches (e.g., 0x15A7E4 instruction rewrite) rather than data -- read context comments before importing as symbols."
        ],
