      {
        "topic": "Sweep for existing Brave Fencer Musashi (SLUS-00726) decompilation, disassembly, modding, and RE work beyond TCRF/AiroRom",
        "key_facts": [
          "NO matching decompilation project exists for BFM anywhere public (as of 2026-06-10). GitHub repo search for 'brave fencer' returns exactly 3 repos (total_count=3): AegeusEvander/Brave-Fencer-Musashi-AP-World, Aalaizah/FencerPop, sherpa-code/YUSA (an Unreal fan prototype, not RE). Searches 'musashi psx', 'musashi playstation', 'musashiden' return 0 repos. BFM is absent from decomp.dev/projects, absent from the awesome-game-decompilations PS1 list (32 PS1/PS2 games, no BFM), has no decomp.wiki/Decompedia page, and no Google-indexed decomp.me scratch. No public splat config or symbol list exists. This project would be first.",
          "BIGGEST REUSABLE FIND: github.com/AegeusEvander/Brave-Fencer-Musashi-AP-World — an actively developed Archipelago randomizer apworld (29 releases, latest v0.6.0 May 2026, last commit 2026-05-20). client.py (300 KB) is a goldmine of verified USA+JP RAM addresses and runtime MIPS code patches. Files: client.py, locations.py (52KB), progression_state.py (61KB), rules.py (44KB), portals.py, items.py, options.py, store_info.py, dialog_locations.py, jp_encoding.py, plus patch/{en,jp}/*.bin precompiled code hooks (fixBinchoID, fixChests, updateProgression, writeBincho, version).",
          "Key USA RAM addresses from AP-world client.py (BizHawk MAIN_RAM offsets; add 0x80000000 for PSX virtual addr): current HP 0x078EB4 (u16); current location/map ID 0x0B9A08 (u16, map IDs like 0x1010 town, 0x2018 interiors, 0x3000+ dungeons); main-menu flag 0x0B99DE; Bincho rescue flags 0x0AE671 (9 bytes); Minku 0x0AE650; chest flags 0x0AE651 (5 bytes); toy flags 0x0BA21B (43 bytes); Scrolls+Legendary Armor 0x0AE64A (3 bytes); Geezer flag 0x0BA1F3; Steamwood status 0x0BA285; zone-loaded/portal-destination control block 0x075400; game-version identifier byte at 0x00BA94. JP (Musashiden) data addresses = USA minus 0xEA0 (zone block minus 0xE70).",
          "AP-world client.py also documents in-RAM CODE patch sites proving overlay/code layout knowledge: 0x15A7E4 town-ID check ('andi $v0 $s0 0x4000' patched, JP equivalent noted as 0x8015AB20, JP code delta +0x2A8); 0x14BCF8 max-BP calculation (nop'd 'addu $v0,$a1', JP delta +0x2D0); 0x13F430 scroll cursor fix (JP delta +0x344); 0x18E096 entrance index (JP delta +0xE8); GPU VRAM hair palette at GPURAM 0x86AC4. Client hooks/patches are applied live over BizHawk's connector_bizhawk_generic.lua — no ISO patching since apworld v0.3.0.",
          "Complete GameShark address set extracted from libretro-database cht file 'Brave Fencer Musashi (USA, Japan) (GameShark).cht' (35 cheats): HP 0x078EB2/0x078EB4, BP 0x078EB6/0x078EB8, cash 0x078E8E, EXP 0x078F08, in-game clock 0x078E7C (2 words), tiredness 0x078EA6, stat block Body 0x078EE4 / Body-EXP 0x078EE8 / Mind 0x078EEC / Mind-EXP 0x078EF0 / FUS 0x078EF4 / FUS-EXP 0x078EF8 / LUM 0x078EFC / LUM-EXP 0x078F00 (max value 0x031B), techs bitfield 0x0AE658, Legendary Armor 0x0AE64B-4C, rescue-complete flags 0x0BA1F8-0x0BA21A, map modifier 0x0B9A08, controller/joker 0x078DCA, jump/physics code 0x126B8E + 0x126C00 + 0x126D98 (overlay region), music ID 0x0AE640, raft logs 0x0BA286, Steamwood valve timer 0x1204A8, model tilt 0x0AFAF9/FB/FD, 'weirdness' 0x0AFB0C, shading 0x0A63F3. GameHacking.org pages: NTSC-U gamehacking.org/game/88529, NTSC-J gamehacking.org/game/93476 (both Cloudflare-blocked to scripts; addresses above recovered via the libretro mirror).",
          "Asset/format RE that exists: (a) 'Brave Fencer extractor' on romhacking.net/utilities/939/ — data extractor/decompressor for the game's .CD container files, source code included, dated 2013-03-16; (b) AiroRom wiki (github.com/pleonex/AiroRom/wiki/Brave-fencer-Musashi, repo archived Dec 2022) documents the LZSS-variant compression as commented MIPS R3000 asm: 1024-byte (2^10) ring buffer, 10-bit back-reference index, bit-flag tokens, 5-state resumable state machine — no header/format spec, no repacker; (c) models are TMD-based per vg-resource ripping threads (textures don't auto-transfer).",
          "Translation hacks prove text pipeline was cracked before: French patch by Inexpugnable/CRHack hosted on TRAF (traf.romhack.org/?p=patchs&pid=902), dated 2011-06-24, ~90% complete main-script-only — tools never published. Romhacking.net forum thread '[PSX] Brave Fencer Musashi' (romhacking.net/forum/index.php?topic=26396.0) exists but is Cloudflare-blocked to all fetch methods tried.",
          "Two US prototypes are public via Hidden Palace Project Deluge + archive.org: 'Brave Fencer Musashi (Aug 31, 1998 prototype)' — boots to a scene/area-select debug menu instead of the main menu (hiddenpalace.org/Brave_Fencer_Musashi_(Aug_31,_1998_prototype), archive.org/details/BraveFencerMusashiAug311998prototype) and 'Sep 8, 1998 prototype' — late localization build (archive.org/details/BraveFencerMusashiSep81998prototype). Useful for diffing and possibly less-stripped code.",
          "Speedrun community exists: speedrun.com/bfm (API game id j1l8q76g, series 'The Legend of Musashi' gnyjgkxn), 9 guides (mostly route notes, e.g. Glitchless Any% and Pianoman7117's Perfect Ending Google Doc), active Discord linked from the game page. No published RAM-level technical docs found in guides — the deep knowledge likely lives in their Discord and in the Archipelago Discord (AP world author AegeusEvander).",
          "Randomizer ecosystem details: BFM AP world requires BizHawk >= 2.7 with Archipelago's connector_bizhawk_generic.lua, Archipelago >= 0.4.4, NTSC BIN/CUE of the game; supports BOTH USA and JP discs (region auto-detected via identifier at 0x00BA94). Companion tracker: github.com/Aalaizah/FencerPop (PopTracker pack); the AP repo's tracker/ dir has full location JSON (106 KB locations.json) and annotated area maps. Archipelago wiki page: archipelago.miraheze.org/wiki/Brave_Fencer_Musashi (Cloudflare-blocked to scripts).",
          "DataCrystal has NO BFM content: datacrystal.tcrf.net/wiki/Brave_Fencer_Musashi returns 404; the ROM/RAM-map links on neoromhacking.net/gamepage.php?id=1810 are auto-generated stubs. NeoRHDN lists only the one extractor utility for the game.",
          "Local context: the working repo Z:\\Storage\\git\\BFM-decomp already contains a redump-style dump 'Brave Fencer Musashi (USA)' with Track 1 (data, 364,846,944 bytes) + Tracks 2-4 (CDDA audio) + .cue — matches redump layout used by the psx-cue-sbi-collection cue sheet."
        ],
        "workflow_steps": [
          "Mine github.com/AegeusEvander/Brave-Fencer-Musashi-AP-World client.py for every literal address and comment; convert MAIN_RAM offsets to 0x8000xxxx PSX addresses and seed the Ghidra symbol table / future splat symbol_addrs.txt with them (HP, location ID, flag arrays, the four patched code sites).",
          "Import the 35-cheat GameShark set from libretro-database (raw.githubusercontent.com/libretro/libretro-database/master/cht/Sony%20-%20PlayStation/Brave%20Fencer%20Musashi%20(USA,%20Japan)%20(GameShark).cht) as additional data labels (player stat block 0x078Exx-0x078Fxx, flag region 0x0AE6xx/0x0BA1xx-0x0BA2xx, overlay code 0x126xxx).",
          "Manually download (browser, Cloudflare blocks scripts) the 'Brave Fencer extractor' from romhacking.net/utilities/939/ and read its included source for the .CD container + decompression format; cross-check against the AiroRom wiki LZSS-variant asm (1024-byte window, 10-bit index, 5-state machine).",
          "Manually read romhacking.net forum thread topic=26396 and the GameHacking.org pages 88529/93476 in a browser; also manually search decomp.me for 'musashi' scratches (API is Cloudflare-blocked) to close the last verification gap.",
          "Download both 1998 prototypes from archive.org (Aug 31 build has a scene-select debug menu) for binary diffing against retail SLUS-00726 and to hunt for leftover symbols/debug strings.",
          "Contact points if needed: AegeusEvander via Archipelago Discord (for the unpublished C sources of the patch/*.bin hooks and version-detection logic) and the speedrun.com/bfm community Discord for glitch/internals knowledge.",
          "Use the JP-vs-US address deltas encoded in client.py (data -0xEA0, code +0xE8/+0x2A8/+0x2D0/+0x344 depending on region of the binary) as a cross-version sanity check when naming functions in Ghidra."
        ],
