        "windows_vs_linux": "All findings in this sweep are platform-neutral (web resources, Python apworld, BizHawk is Windows-native). Note for the host machine: gh CLI is not installed; PowerShell Invoke-RestMethod worked fine for GitHub API and raw.githubusercontent.com, but romhacking.net, gamehacking.org, decomp.me, miraheze, datacrystal.tcrf.net, and archive.vg-resource.com all return Cloudflare 403 to scripted fetches and need a real browser.",
        "risks_gotchas": [
          "AP-world addresses are BizHawk MAIN_RAM domain offsets, not PSX virtual addresses — add 0x80000000 (e.g. HP 0x078EB4 -> 0x80078EB4).",
          "Addresses in the 0x126xxx / 0x13F-0x18E xxx ranges are inside dynamically loaded overlay/code regions — they are only valid in specific game states; do not treat them as static EXE symbols until the overlay system is mapped.",
          "License of Brave-Fencer-Musashi-AP-World is not stated in any fetched file (README is 0.1 KB; no LICENSE file in the tree) — raw addresses/facts are fine to reuse, but verify before copying code; the C sources for patch/{en,jp}/*.bin hooks are NOT in the repo at all.",
          "Negative results have one verification gap: decomp.me could not be queried directly (Cloudflare challenge on /api/scratch?search=musashi) — Google site-search found nothing, but do a one-time manual browser check. GitHub CODE search (vs repo search) was also not possible unauthenticated; grep.app was rate-limited (429) throughout.",
          "romhacking.net forum thread topic=26396 ('[PSX] Brave Fencer Musashi') could not be read by any method (direct, UA-spoofed, r.jina.ai) — unknown content, could contain format docs; read manually.",
          "Two GameShark codes in the libretro cht look typo-prone: 'Charging Bar Always Full' is listed as 80078EEBE (9 digits — probably 0x078EEB or 0x078EBE) — verify in-emulator before trusting.",
          "The game has JP (Musashiden) and US releases with shifted addresses; prototypes will shift again — keep region/build tags on every symbol imported from these sources."
        ],
